WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.160
How do you measure what a hidden nephron filters, takes back, or adds?

2
00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:10.260
Three measurements turn that work into numbers: micropuncture, clearance, and

3
00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:11.540
freezing-point osmometry.

4
00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:14.200
Start with micropuncture.

5
00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:20.580
Under a microscope, a fine glass pipette draws a tiny drop from Bowman's capsule,

6
00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:22.360
the cup around the filter.

7
00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:27.100
A solute there but missing from bladder urine was taken back.

8
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:31.060
Without a pipette, blood and urine read the kidney.

9
00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:37.240
Clearance equals urine concentration times urine flow, divided by plasma

10
00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:43.720
concentration. No plasma is wiped clean; it is the plasma volume holding one

11
00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:44.920
minute's excreted amount.

12
00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:50.240
Inulin is freely filtered, neither reabsorbed nor secreted.

13
00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:57.260
So its clearance equals the glomerular filtration rate, or GFR, the plasma filtered

14
00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:58.260
per minute.

15
00:00:58.917 --> 00:01:01.537
Take illustrative adult human numbers.

16
00:01:02.977 --> 00:01:08.357
Urine inulin is 30 mg/mL; urine flow is 2.0 mL/min.

17
00:01:09.817 --> 00:01:13.417
Plasma inulin is 0.50 mg/mL.

18
00:01:14.657 --> 00:01:22.417
30 × 2.0 is 60. 60 / 0.50 gives 120 mL/min.

19
00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:26.590
Other clearances read the tubule against inulin.

20
00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:35.150
Now predict. Another freely filtered substance has a clearance of 300 mL/min.

21
00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:39.130
Did the tubule reabsorb it on net, or secrete it?

22
00:01:44.583 --> 00:01:46.503
The tubule secreted it on net.

23
00:01:47.823 --> 00:01:52.283
More leaves in urine than filtration alone could carry, so cells added extra.

24
00:01:53.503 --> 00:01:56.663
At 1 mL/min, most was reabsorbed.

25
00:01:57.863 --> 00:01:59.723
Next, how do we measure concentration?

26
00:02:00.983 --> 00:02:05.063
Osmolality counts dissolved particles per kilogram of water.

27
00:02:06.363 --> 00:02:10.083
One sodium chloride makes two ions; one urea stays one.

28
00:02:11.463 --> 00:02:16.703
Extra particles lower the freezing point, so freezing-point osmometry reads

29
00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:19.603
osmolality from the temperature where a sample freezes.

30
00:02:20.817 --> 00:02:25.797
Creatinine, a muscle waste, is slightly secreted, so its clearance tends to

31
00:02:25.797 --> 00:02:32.837
overestimate GFR. Osmosis follows effective osmolality: only solutes that cannot

32
00:02:32.837 --> 00:02:34.097
cross a membrane freely.

33
00:02:35.377 --> 00:02:40.817
Freezing point also counts urea, which crosses cell membranes fairly readily and

34
00:02:40.817 --> 00:02:42.297
draws little water out of cells.

35
00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:45.690
These methods unlocked three findings.

36
00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:51.250
In 1924, Wearn and Richards micropunctured a frog kidney.

37
00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:57.770
Capsular fluid held sugar and chloride, no protein found; bladder urine held no

38
00:02:57.770 --> 00:03:02.650
sugar. That fitted a filter followed by reabsorption, in the frog.

39
00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:10.130
In 1951, Wirz, Hargitay, and Kuhn measured freezing points of rat kidney slices.

40
00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:15.670
Osmolality climbed from the cortex down to the papilla, the inner tip.

41
00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:21.730
A countercurrent multiplier, a hairpin loop with opposite flows, predicted that

42
00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:22.730
gradient.

43
00:03:23.267 --> 00:03:28.287
In 2016, Zimmerman, Knight, and colleagues studied water-restricted mice.

44
00:03:29.747 --> 00:03:32.467
Thirst neurons quieted within one minute of drinking.

45
00:03:33.727 --> 00:03:39.147
Yet plasma osmolality, measured by freezing-point osmometry, stayed raised five

46
00:03:39.147 --> 00:03:43.687
minutes later. So the fast signal comes with water going in.

47
00:03:44.687 --> 00:03:49.027
But blood was sampled at set times, so a small early change could be missed.
